      "writtenOn": "2014-12-09T13:53:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of making null illegal here, can we reserve it to mean \"whatever proxy this network specified\"? That way we\u0027d address all the use cases:\n\n  1. openConnection(url) -\u003e global proxy, else network\u0027s proxy\n  2. openConnection(url, null) -\u003e network\u0027s proxy\n  3. openConnection(url, proxy) -\u003e specified proxy\n  4. openConnection(url, Proxy.NO_PROXY) -\u003e no proxy\n\nWith this CL, apps that want to do #3 have to do:\n\n    LinkProperties lp \u003d getLinkProperties(network);\n    Proxy proxy \u003d lp.getHttpProxy();\n    URLConnection conn \u003d network.openConnection(url, proxy);\n\nwhich seems like something we could do for them.",
      "revId": "31b560ca99c63b70cc12f95f3910f433dfcd94fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
